From 7efa7b787ca3ffef920276004553a12848b6da43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 11:52:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 39/75] wm: render a translucent dialog task as one centered
 modal (ARC)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Complements 0038. A floating activity in its OWN translucent task — e.g.
PackageInstaller, whose transparent no-UI root (DeleteStagedFileOnResult)
isn't floating but whose visible PackageInstallerActivity on top is — must
not be split per-window by IS_FLOATING_ACTIVITY: it has multiple concentric
windows that would fragment into separate modals.

- ActivityRecord.setInitialSurfaceControlProperties: gate
  IS_FLOATING_ACTIVITY on !task.isTranslucent(), so it only fires when there
  is a real opaque host beneath (e.g. the brightness dialog over Settings).
  A translucent task (no opaque host) is skipped.
- Task.setTaskMetadata: also set METADATA_IS_DIALOG when the task is
  translucent AND its top activity is floating. The translucent gate keeps a
  normal opaque app from being flagged when it merely shows a dialog activity
  (the 0037 concern). The whole task then composites into one centered
  frameless modal instead of fragmenting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I080c453b952939539a21692247da58f5041ecee6
---
 .../com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java | 11 +++++++-
 .../core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java | 26 ++++++++++++-------
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java
index 2c86ebbca4db..a94acd20f222 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java
@@ -7549,7 +7549,16 @@ final class ActivityRecord extends WindowToken implements WindowManagerService.A
         // unions its display-centered bounds into the host footprint, auto-
         // expanding the host window. Mark the activity's own surface so the
         // compositor can split it into its own modal window instead.
-        if (info != null && task != null && !isRootOfTask() && usesFloatingTheme()) {
+        //
+        // Only do this when the task has a real OPAQUE host beneath (e.g. the
+        // brightness dialog over Settings). A *translucent* task — one with no
+        // opaque activity, e.g. PackageInstaller (its no-UI DeleteStagedFileOnResult
+        // root isn't floating, but the whole task is the dialog) — must NOT be
+        // split per-activity: it has multiple windows that would fragment into
+        // separate modals. Such a task is flagged IsDialogTask instead (see
+        // Task.setTaskMetadata) and composited as one centered modal.
+        if (info != null && task != null && !isRootOfTask() && usesFloatingTheme()
+                && !task.isTranslucent(null /* starting */)) {
             b.setMetadata(SurfaceControl.METADATA_IS_FLOATING_ACTIVITY, 1);
         }
         super.setInitialSurfaceControlProperties(b);
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java
index 2166eade3dca..2b98b4bfe0fd 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/Task.java
@@ -3119,15 +3119,23 @@ class Task extends TaskFragment {
                         == ApplicationInfo.CATEGORY_GAME) {
             b.setMetadata(METADATA_IS_GAME, 1);
         }
-        // A task is a dialog task only when its ROOT activity uses a floating
-        // theme — i.e. the whole task is a standalone dialog (PackageInstaller,
-        // permission prompts). Checking the top activity instead flags a normal
-        // app the moment it shows a dialog-themed activity on top: the task
-        // metadata propagates to all child layers, and the Chrome-side composer
-        // latches the entire app task into a modal overlay. setTaskMetadata is
-        // re-run on makeAnimationLeash (the dialog-open transition), so the
-        // top-activity check would flip mid-animation and stick.
-        if (isDialogTask(getRootActivity())) {
+        // A task is a dialog task when its ROOT activity uses a floating theme —
+        // i.e. the whole task is a standalone dialog (permission prompts) —
+        // OR when the task is translucent (no opaque activity) and its TOP
+        // activity is floating. The latter covers PackageInstaller: its root is
+        // a transparent no-UI activity (DeleteStagedFileOnResult), not floating,
+        // but the visible PackageInstallerActivity on top is — so the whole task
+        // is effectively the dialog and must composite into one centered modal
+        // rather than fragment per-window via IS_FLOATING_ACTIVITY.
+        //
+        // The translucent gate is what keeps a normal app from being flagged the
+        // moment it shows a dialog-themed activity on top (an opaque app task is
+        // never translucent): checking the top activity alone would flip a normal
+        // app into a modal mid-transition (setTaskMetadata re-runs on
+        // makeAnimationLeash). A translucent task has no opaque content to lose.
+        if (isDialogTask(getRootActivity())
+                || (isTranslucent(null /* starting */)
+                        && isDialogTask(getTopNonFinishingActivity()))) {
             b.setMetadata(METADATA_IS_DIALOG, 1);
         }
         if (getActivityType() == ACTIVITY_TYPE_HOME) {
